{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity","id":57794,"title":"Epic Dexterity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-25T17:58:34-08:00","id":57794,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Epic Dexterity","content":"So I'm looking at running a Hero-tier Scion game, and I'm trying to learn the ruleset and suchforth, since none of us have played it before. And while I like the idea of Epic Attributes, Epic Dexterity does seem to be the be-all and end-all with regard to physical combat. It affects offensive capability through both being more likely to hit and increasing likely thresholds, thus increasing damage (albeit not as much as Epic Strength would in the same context), and makes you harder to hit, and less likely to be hit hard through decreasing the likely thresholds of incoming attacks. This seems to the point that <i>not</i> putting points into ED seems like a very bad move in terms of character creation, which of course is kind of silly in terms of character concepts and suchforth.<br /> <br /> Is the issue in actual play as bad as it seems it might be? And if so, has anyone come up with a workable houserule solution?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T18:08:01-08:00","id":57798,"title":"","content":"No, that's quite true. Your observations are accurate. This is a flaw with Dexterity itself, that is only exacerbated by Epic Dexterity. <br /> <br /> Some people have said that they do not have additional attack roll successes add to damage, but that still leaves Dexterity as improving both your offense (hitting at all) and your defense (dodge/parry/block). It's an issue because Strength is Damage, Stamina is Soak but Dexterity is both Accuracy <b>and</b> Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T19:04:33-08:00","id":57824,"title":"","content":"Indeed. This is one of the biggest hurdles the 2E crew is going to have to overcome.<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure what the solution to this problem is. Dex makes sense as determining both Accuracy and Dodge capability, not to mention Movement Speed.<br /> <br /> I suppose one can remove the &quot;Threshold successes adding to Damage&quot; thing. But what do you use to replace Dex as the &quot;Accuracy and Dodge&quot; Attribute? What is the answer to this problem? How DO the devs give us a system using the same Attribute set without letting Dex once again dominate in importance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T20:53:58-08:00","id":57877,"title":"","content":"What about if you removed the effects of Epic Dexterity from attack pools? It's a bit strange, I know, but not without precedent: Mobility penalties in Exalted usually don't apply to attack pools, but to everything else involving Dex. Then you'd still have the defensive capability of ED, but it would stop it flowing onto damage, at least, and for soak Epic Stamina would be better (coming in after rolling, rather than simply reducing threshold successes)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T00:15:33-08:00","id":57955,"title":"","content":"problem is if you remove epic dex from attack pools then high dex scions, gods, titans are unhitable as it would still add to defense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T01:12:47-08:00","id":57972,"title":"","content":"Something I've done with the cWOD, which suffers a similar though less pronounced issue with Dexterity in combat, is to allow you to make hand-to-hand attacks with Strength or Dexterity. Strength based attacks don't add extra successes to damage but still benefit from increased damage via high Strength. Dexterity based attacks add extra successes to damage, but without high Strength are less reliable for doing high damage/overcoming tanks.<br /> <br /> If you're keeping to a Hero level game, I can see this working fairly well with Scion (I'm not sure it really works if you keep to the escalating numbers of higher level Scion). Dex is still superior if you're just going to invest in one physical Attribute for combat, but if you're going to be sinking points into multiple combat Attributes, it makes Strength/Stamina builds more appealing because you can tank and still reliably score hits on higher DV targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T03:00:28-08:00","id":57999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=57824#post57824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. This is one of the biggest hurdles the 2E crew is going to have to overcome.<br /> <br /> I'm not even sure what the solution to this problem is. Dex makes sense as determining both Accuracy and Dodge capability, not to mention Movement Speed.<br /> <br /> I suppose one can remove the &quot;Threshold successes adding to Damage&quot; thing. But what do you use to replace Dex as the &quot;Accuracy and Dodge&quot; Attribute? What is the answer to this problem? How DO the devs give us a system using the same Attribute set without letting Dex once again dominate in importance?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're writing a rules system from the ground up, they may introduce new stats. For example, they may introduce Dexterity for Attacks and Agility for Defence? I know this isn't ideal, but it's just a random brain storm example <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/945-space-monkey","name":"Space Monkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T03:25:04-08:00","id":58003,"title":"","content":"Alternatively allow Strength or Int to determine extra damage and Wits or Dex to determine attacks and defence pools. Manipulation or Charisma arguably too...we're talking about super powered beings here, I could see someone being smart enough and quick witted enough to spot the weak point and hitting it for massive damage. Manipulation to trick your opponent into creating a weakness for you to exploit...Charisma for damage I'm less sold on though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T16:26:56-08:00","id":58390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=58003#post58003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively allow Strength or Int to determine extra damage and Wits or Dex to determine attacks and defence pools. Manipulation or Charisma arguably too...we're talking about super powered beings here, I could see someone being smart enough and quick witted enough to spot the weak point and hitting it for massive damage. Manipulation to trick your opponent into creating a weakness for you to exploit...Charisma for damage I'm less sold on though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charisma could be used to distract the opponent probably, for that matter Epic Appearance would probably work for that too. All sorts of things could theoretically be useful really. <br /> <br /> It gives me the glimmering of an idea where the player would construct a custom attack and defense package from components that make sense for the character concept but I am not that good at puzzling together rules crunch like that to make a house rules set for it unfortunately. It may seem odd to use nontraditional stats and skills for combat but the reality in most gaming sessions is that if the &quot;non-fighter types&quot; cannot fight as well or at least nearly as well as the fighter types in SOME way (as well as the fighters having something to contribute to the non-combat scenes) then half the group is bored while the other half plays and it flip-flops back and forth which is not as good as everyone involved most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T18:14:16-08:00","id":58437,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of being able to use just about any Attribute to contribute to attack, means any build can be useful in combat provided they can justify how Appearance can help them punch the Hydra in the throats. Makes the Boons a lot more important in distinguishing between particular characters, which is good: it <i>seems</i> to me that they're really more of an afterthought in the RAW. Nice, by all means, but often kind of superfluous next to the automatic successes, at least at the Hero level, for the most part.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I've flipped through the Demigod and God books a bit, looks almost like the game breaks down a bit. When a lot of your powers are variants on the theme of &quot;what I want happens&quot;, it makes it difficult to enjoy. So I'm probably going to keep it to the Hero level for the foreseeable future, It might be fun to do the higher-levels for a one-off or similar, but for extended I prefer there to be an element of difficulty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=57955#post57955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">problem is if you remove epic dex from attack pools then high dex scions, gods, titans are unhitable as it would still add to defense</div> </div> </div> </div>I did notice that a lot of the antagonists have ED to one extent or another, which makes their DVs way higher than can be realistically expected to hit. So I've more or less scrapped that idea. But if using Strength or Dex to attack <i>might</i> offset that a bit?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T23:26:42-08:00","id":58547,"title":"","content":"<b>Allow characters to roll their Strength when attacking with Brawl or Melee.</b> This very minor change goes a long way towards making Str/Sta characters viable when compared against Dex/Sta characters.<br /> <br /> You create a rock, paper, scissor situation where Strength beats Stamina, Stamina beats Dexterity, and Dexterity beats Strength more often then not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:58:34-08:00","id":59037,"title":"","content":"How does stam beat dex in that situation? Doesnt it just make it only strength vs stam really?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T13:58:39-08:00","id":59106,"title":"","content":"Basically, the extra successes impact on damage is generally not enough to deal with the increased soak.<br /> <br /> As Scion isn't as &quot;touch of death&quot; happy as Exalted tends to be, there are very few ways to take out someone that's got really high soak besides really high damage output. Thus Stamina based defense is stronger in most ways than Dexterity based defense. And Dexterity alone is rarely good enough to break through an equal investment in tanking.<br /> <br /> I do think that simply making it Strength or Dexterity is problematic. Hence my version posted earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T19:27:37-08:00","id":59389,"title":"","content":"It might be possible to simply reduce attacks to one single roll: an Attack Roll. Net successes are applied directly as damage, which is then soaked. Make Soak the <i>only</i> form of defense, then just say that Strength rolls are for hand-to-hand combat and Dexterity rolls are for ranged combat. Now every Physical Attribute has <i>exactly</i> one function and no more. It works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T20:42:52-08:00","id":59447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=59389#post59389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be possible to simply reduce attacks to one single roll: an Attack Roll. Net successes are applied directly as damage, which is then soaked. Make Soak the <i>only</i> form of defense, then just say that Strength rolls are for hand-to-hand combat and Dexterity rolls are for ranged combat. Now every Physical Attribute has <i>exactly</i> one function and no more. It works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like an unholy blending of nWoD and 40k rules, neither of which are situations I find entirely fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T20:58:59-08:00","id":59459,"title":"","content":"I was actually thinking it was pretty close to the D6 system, which uses Strength for hand-to-hand and Agility for ranged, but has set values for damage that are not determined by your stats at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:14:18-08:00","id":59550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=59447#post59447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like an unholy blending of nWoD and 40k rules, neither of which are situations I find entirely fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I have no interest in making Scion too nWOD like (though I like the nWOD system), the nWOD iteration of the ST system is probably the best at keeping a decent balance of the importance of multiple Attributes in combat. A character that dumps everything into Dexterity can be effective, but it isn't likely to be as good as a more balanced investment in combat related Attributes. The only real exception is guns, but the nWOD is modelling a more lethal take on modern day combat; so guns are pretty damned deadly in the nWOD and it really doesn't matter which Attribute you use for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T01:04:56-08:00","id":59606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=59550#post59550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I have no interest in making Scion too nWOD like (though I like the nWOD system), the nWOD iteration of the ST system is probably the best at keeping a decent balance of the importance of multiple Attributes in combat. A character that dumps everything into Dexterity can be effective, but it isn't likely to be as good as a more balanced investment in combat related Attributes. The only real exception is guns, but the nWOD is modelling a more lethal take on modern day combat; so guns are pretty damned deadly in the nWOD and it really doesn't matter which Attribute you use for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good point, it's just that nWoD's combining of attack and damage leads to some pretty stupid situations (like the best decision being giving the biggest gun to the least skilled character), and I'd really, really prefer to avoid replicating those.<br /> <br /> What if we change how Epic Attributes work entirely? Rather than making them give auto-successes (which is kind of silly, really), they add dice (like, Dex 3 and ED 2 means 5 dice), as well as being sources for Boons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T08:34:23-08:00","id":59843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=59606#post59606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You make a good point, it's just that nWoD's combining of attack and damage leads to some pretty stupid situations (like the best decision being giving the biggest gun to the least skilled character), and I'd really, really prefer to avoid replicating those.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to at least look at the GMC (free) rules update thing. nWOD combat is still single roll, but works more like what Telgar suggested (you roll to attack, which generates a damage amount, that gets reduced by armor, and then the target takes what's left). The Str 1/Dex 1/Firearms 0 Granny with a shotgun being stupid dangerous is very dead in the current incarnation of the rules (not that's anyone with a shotgun isn't something to worry about because a lucky hit with a shotgun sucks for the target, but she's starting with a -1 dice-pool and a -4 init as is now).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if we change how Epic Attributes work entirely? Rather than making them give auto-successes (which is kind of silly, really), they add dice (like, Dex 3 and ED 2 means 5 dice), as well as being sources for Boons? </div> </div> </div>Changing the scaling of the system is a fairly common approach to Scion.<br /> <br /> The problem with more dice, is that the dice pool size gets very large, very fast. Hucking 14-16 dice is pretty cumbersome and isn't particularly more beneficial than rolling 10 dice with +2-3 auto-successes.<br /> <br /> And even if you changed it to dice, or reduced how fast the scaling increases, the inherent &quot;Dex is the king of combat&quot; problems still remain. Dex might not be king by as far a margin, but it remains none-the-less if that's all you change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T14:29:22-08:00","id":60128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=59606#post59606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if we change how Epic Attributes work entirely? Rather than making them give auto-successes (which is kind of silly, really), they add dice (like, Dex 3 and ED 2 means 5 dice), as well as being sources for Boons?</div> </div> </div> </div>After a certain point, you lose some degree of variation found in smaller dice pools. While it'd be pretty conceivable for a pool of 7 dice to result in no successes or in 5 successes, once you hit 30 dice you're going to be pretty close to 15 pretty consistently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T17:11:05-08:00","id":60242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=59843#post59843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might want to at least look at the GMC (free) rules update thing. nWOD combat is still single roll, but works more like what Telgar suggested (you roll to attack, which generates a damage amount, that gets reduced by armor, and then the target takes what's left). The Str 1/Dex 1/Firearms 0 Granny with a shotgun being stupid dangerous is very dead in the current incarnation of the rules (not that's anyone with a shotgun isn't something to worry about because a lucky hit with a shotgun sucks for the target, but she's starting with a -1 dice-pool and a -4 init as is now).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've seen, and I like (for the most part). Not entirely thrilled with how they've reworked experience with Beats, and how those are gained, but that's a different conversation entirely.<br /> <br /> And the difference (as I see it, it's all theory for me so I could well be wrong) is that when rolling 15 dice, you can still fail. It's unlikely, sure, but we've all seen it happen, particularly when you need more than one success as you do in combat. But adding successes completely rules out botches occurring, and makes it much easier to succeed, because you only need to roll eg 2 or 3 successes, rather than 6. Some very quick mental arithmatic says that if 8+ is the successes on a d10, you've got (roughly) a 30% success rate, which means one success is 'worth' roughly 3 dice. So rather than getting 2 successes (6 dice equivalent), you get 2 dice.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Dex is still kind of...central, which this fix doesn't address. And it seems silly to make Dex do dice when everything else does successes (plus I would think would shift EStam into the breaking Epic Attribute for combat).<br /> <br /> Hell, even Lunar in Exalted need to activate an Attribute excellency to get this kind of benefit, and they're pretty awesome. Maybe say that to benefit from your Epic Attributes you need to spend a point of Legend, or maybe an amount equal to your rating, or something? Makes sense thematically, since you're tapping into your godly nature and suchforth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=60128#post60128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After a certain point, you lose some degree of variation found in smaller dice pools. While it'd be pretty conceivable for a pool of 7 dice to result in no successes or in 5 successes, once you hit 30 dice you're going to be pretty close to 15 pretty consistently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it won't work with the higher levels, I'm focussing purely on a Hero-tier solution. The issues with Epic Attributes at the Demigod and God level really are beyond fixing, in my opinion. powers, you really need t<br /> <br /> So on a Hero-tier, say Dex of 5 and ED of 3 would give a total Dex dice pool of 8. Powerful, yes, of course: you've clearly hyper-focussed. But that would result in a base DV of at most 8 or 9 (can't remember if it rounds up or down). Whereas with the current setup, same stats results in a DV of 11 if I've worked that out right ((5 Dex + 5 Athl + 4 Legend/2)+4 = 14/2 + 4 = 11). 8 or 9 is a very high DV, true, but 11 is even worse. But the difference is pretty small in practical terms, and both get pretty insane once you bring in Untouchable Opponent to double it to 16 or 22 for the scene.<br /> <br /> Hmmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T10:32:49-08:00","id":60896,"title":"","content":"Perhaps one possibility is sort of splitting in half the Capacity of Epic Dex by making it so you have to distribute your extra successes instead of applying all of it for every roll? Say you have 10 auto-successes, you could in one put 10 in attack, zero in defense, next round 4 in attack, 6 in defense and so on. It is a bit fiddly but not too hard to keep track.<br /> <br /> If even the mundane version of Dex is bothering you, it might be worth doing the same with the dice gained from it<br /> <br /> You can even make things &quot;fair&quot; and say that such distribution applies to all Epics during combat...it just so happens that it is very rare that you will need anything other than dexterity playing double duty like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T16:27:37-08:00","id":61143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=60896#post60896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps one possibility is sort of splitting in half the Capacity of Epic Dex by making it so you have to distribute your extra successes instead of applying all of it for every roll? Say you have 10 auto-successes, you could in one put 10 in attack, zero in defense, next round 4 in attack, 6 in defense and so on. It is a bit fiddly but not too hard to keep track.<br /> <br /> If even the mundane version of Dex is bothering you, it might be worth doing the same with the dice gained from it<br /> <br /> You can even make things &quot;fair&quot; and say that such distribution applies to all Epics during combat...it just so happens that it is very rare that you will need anything other than dexterity playing double duty like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is actually a good idea. Character will have to redefine where they go say at the start of their turn, and while it is still doing double duty, the relative drop makes it a lot more balanced with the other EAtt.<br /> <br /> The mundane version of Dex doesn't bother me as much, really. I mean, it's still central, but at least the benefits are linear, not exponential like they are with other EAtt. So the effects are a bit less...broken, at least a the Hero tier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T21:31:34-08:00","id":61987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=59459#post59459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually thinking it was pretty close to the D6 system, which uses Strength for hand-to-hand and Agility for ranged, but has set values for damage that are not determined by your stats at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strength adds to unarmed and melee attacks, unless the weapon wouldn't make meaningful use of it somehow (i.e. lightsabers) in D6.<br /> <br /> I'm not enamored of the solution myself, bluntly. I think simply changing it so you make an attack based on Dexterity OR Strength, whichever is lowest for melee attacks and Dexterity OR Perception, whichever is lowest for ranged attacks. (And derive defenses from Dex OR Wits, lower.)<br /> <br /> So yes, you can sort of min-max. But not really. Doesn't significantly change the game, except to make the Scions of war gods much more questionable defensively, which strikes me as an acceptable compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T23:57:00-08:00","id":63798,"title":"","content":"You could always make Perception your offensive stat (accuracy), and your Dexterity your defensive stat (evasion).<br /> Actually... Wits = Initiative, Perception = Accuracy, Dexterity = Defence, Strength = Damage. This pretty much prevents any one Attribute being the go-to for combat. If they had Coordination as an Attribute for manual dexterity, and a different Attribute for overall grace, that might help some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T01:25:24-08:00","id":63822,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure having lots of Attributes you need to buy to be competitive in combat is the way to go. Needing five out of nine Attributes just to be good at one thing seems a tad excessive.<br /> <br /> The issue with Dexterity RAW is that it is so much better than any other option. I think most of us would rather combatants only need to focus on 2-3 Attributes that emphasize a style of fighting, without any particular combo being the clear choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T10:03:23-08:00","id":64087,"title":"","content":"How many attributes you can afford to invest in entirely depends on how much XP your storyteller is handing out. The combat character with a generous storyteller is going to have no issue keeping all three attributes at maximum, and still have some left over to pick up some social or mental attributes. The combat character with a niggardly storyteller is either going to have to be notably less effective at his chosen role, or resign himself to being a one trick pony.<br /> <br /> I have to agree with Heavy Arms on this issue. For me, the ideal amount of investment for a combat character is 2 attributes and I am in favor of system changes that create this result. Investment in a third should provide some meaningful benefit, but it should not be a requirement by any stretch. The current RAW system essentially requires a 3 attribute investment (Strength/Dexterity/Stamina).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 02-04-2014, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T16:48:54-08:00","id":65230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=64087#post64087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with Heavy Arms on this issue. For me, the ideal amount of investment for a combat character is 2 attributes and I am in favor of system changes that create this result. Investment in a third should provide some meaningful benefit, but it should not be a requirement by any stretch. The current RAW system essentially requires a 3 attribute investment (Strength/Dexterity/Stamina).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, maybe I'm misunderstanding, but near I can tell, you only really &quot;need&quot; two Attributes: Dex, and either Strength (doing more damage) or Stamina (taking hits better) depending. Since most have 7ish health boxes, you don't really need both. It's good to have, but not really necessary. The issue is Dex (more precisely, Epic Dex) adds to attack, which means you're more likely to have extra successes (ie, more damage), and ups DV, which means you're less likely to suffer extra successes (ie, less incoming damage, or more effective soak), rendering both EStr and EStam somewhat redundant.<br /> <br /> So, given the situation you've outlined, if you want to be a combat monster, you do only <i>need</i> two Attributes, with the third giving a tangible non-necessary benefit, as RAW. Problem is, EDex is <i>too</i> necessary. Which is what we're trying to address.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T00:31:34-08:00","id":65473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/57794-epic-dexterity?p=65230#post65230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, given the situation you've outlined, if you want to be a combat monster, you do only <i>need</i> two Attributes, with the third giving a tangible non-necessary benefit, as RAW. Problem is, EDex is <i>too</i> necessary. Which is what we're trying to address.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it is certainly true that Dexterity is going to be the epic attribute of choice if you can only invest in a single attribute, the successes you gain on your threshold only translate into dice on the damage roll. This does not maintain parity with an equal investment in Epic Stamina, and you will end up looking like you are having a sissy slap fight!<br /> <br /> There is really not much a dexterity character can do to a stamina character except to ignore her, grapple her, or keep chopping at her until the dice gods bless you with an abundance of 10s. But nobody is <b>JUST</b> an X character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T03:30:30-08:00","id":65529,"title":"","content":"True as far as you take it, but EDex covers both attack and defensive capabilities, while EStam is just defensive and EStr is just offensive. (Obviously this is somewhat academic, as you point out you won't have just EDex <i>or</i> EStam/EStr, you can easily have both, but let's keep it simple to illustrate the point.)<br /> <br /> But more to the point, if your opponent has EDex, which many antagonists do to one degree or another, and you don't, the balance between your attack pool and their DV is immediately swung heavily to their side. So you won't hit them most of the time, and unless you're wielding a powerful weapon probably won't hit them very hard, which results in, as you point out, the slap-fight scenario. Which is just slightly less than epic. EStam accentuates the issue, to be sure, but that can be wiped out by a sufficiently powerful weapon, like a machete or similar. The only way to cancel out the benefit of EDex is to have EDex yourself (assuming the opponent is reasonably set up apart from EDex: reasonable Dex score, few points in Athletics and similar).<br /> <br /> Which, given opponents have it, then it makes characters need it, or their survivability is that much less. And nobody likes their character to die, particularly if it's because you built him for character reasons and didn't come up with a hyper-lithe co-ordinated hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T04:32:37-08:00","id":65555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True as far as you take it, but EDex covers both attack and defensive capabilities, while EStam is just defensive and EStr is just offensive. </div> </div> </div>It is probably better to phrase it like this: Epic Dexterity has 1 Offense and 1 Defense, Epic Stamina has 2 Defense (Soak and Health), and Epic Strength has 1.33 Offense (Grapple and Damage).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you won't hit them most of the time, and unless you're wielding a powerful weapon probably won't hit them very hard, which results in, as you point out, the slap-fight scenario. </div> </div> </div>Hopefully the character with so much epic stamina is engaging in goals that focus on her strengths; leading the epic dexterity character into a hazardous environment, hitting him with non-physical attacks, soaking attacks for her team, or ignoring her opponent entirely and getting on with the mission.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EStam accentuates the issue, to be sure, but that can be wiped out by a sufficiently powerful weapon, like a machete or similar. </div> </div> </div>It would have to be a pretty powerful weapon. Mundane armor goes up faster than mundane weapons (8 die labrys versus 7/10 success armor for example). Stamina has knacks like Body Armor while Dexterity has nothing to directly increase damage to match it. There is also a huge list of ways you can reduce your DV, while only a few ways you can reduce your Soak.<br /> <br /> Stamina is not nearly as flashy of an attribute as Dexterity, but it is absolutely a powerful stat worthy of investing in. <b>Strength is the attribute that needs a little love!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 02-05-2014, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T04:52:43-08:00","id":65562,"title":"","content":"Well, bear in mind I <i>am</i> just running off theory. So it's extremely likely I'm totally wrong.<br /> <br /> From what I can see, though (and we'll assume a rating of 3 for sake of simplicity), EDex gives say an extra 4 to DV (say a Defense rating of 4, to use your terminology), but also gives 4 auto successes to attack (which would be an Offense rating of 4). Ok, that's as it is. However, EStam gives 4 bashing and lethal soak, and 3 agg soak (say a Defense of 4? Agg is pretty situational), with a similar thing with EStr, +4 to Damage.<br /> <br /> I suppose technically you could make the argument that EStam is better at preventing damage than EDex, since it's end-step levels, rather than potential dice, but +4 to DV means, unless the attacker also has EDex to balance it, things are that much harder for them to hit. I'm generalising from Exalted here, but a DV of, what, about 8 or 9? is pretty hard to hit. So EStam just won't come up often. The offensive capabilities of EDex are less certain, but it's certainly nice to have a set number of free successes on your attack roll, which means you'll likely hit a non-EDex user more often than not, particularly given the penalties to DV from, say, attacking and whatnot.<br /> <br /> But say a character instead has EStam 3, just for demonstration sake. Their DV will likely be, say, in the area of 4 or 5? So if they get hit, their soak of 4 does take a lot of damage off the end (damn it, soak coming last really makes this hard to calculate solidly). Their non-armoured soak would be 8B/6L...(assuming 4 Stamina). Damn, nice. So he'll likely be hit more often (although, with a DV of 4 or 5, most mortals wouldn't stand much chance?), but likely won't much care if he is, barring either EStr, a nice weapon, or just lucky rolling.<br /> <br /> But looking at the melee weapons chart, at a quick eyeball something like a third of the weapons have a listed Damage rating of 4 or higher? Assuming a 50% dice-to-damage conversion, we'd need a damage pool of in the realm of 16 bashing or 12 lethal to reliably hurt someone with that soak, or 12B/8L before weapon. Damn.<br /> <br /> Is that a common amount to roll? It seems like a lot, but here my lack of experience stymies me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 02-05-2014, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}